Project: AI Data Analyst Agent (learning project)
Goal

A web app where a user uploads a data file, the agent profiles it, asks a few clarifying questions, then produces charts, insights and recommendations.

Scope
Version 1: CSV only, one file, one user, runs locally.
Version 2: Add JSON and Parquet.
Later: Excel and Word (Word tables are the hardest part).
Out of scope for now: logins, payments, multi-user storage, live database connections.
Stack
Python 3.11+
Streamlit for the UI
DuckDB and pandas for reading and analyzing data
Plotly for charts
Claude API (or OpenAI) for the AI steps
A .env file for the API key (never commit it)
Core rule

The AI never calculates numbers itself. It writes code or SQL, your program runs it, and the results come from that output.

Workflow
Upload: The user uploads a file, and the app reads it into a DataFrame.
Profile (plain code, no AI): For each column, record type, missing %, unique count, min/max, and sample values. Also check for duplicate rows and obvious outliers.
Understand (AI): Send only the profile and about 5 sample rows, not the full data. The AI returns JSON: a guess of what each column means, plus any unclear points.
Clarify (AI + user): The app shows at most 3-4 questions (e.g., “Is amount revenue or cost?”). The answers are saved as a “context” dictionary.
Analyze (AI writes code): The AI gets the profile and context, and returns SQL or Python. The app runs it in a restricted environment and captures the results.
Visualize: The app draws 3-5 charts from the results.
Verify: Check that totals match the original file, and flag any mismatch to the user.
Recommend (AI): Give the AI the verified results and ask for insights, risks, and where to focus. Show the assumptions used.
